@startuml sd_us229
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
title US229 - Sequence Diagram
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
actor "Backoffice Operator" as Actor
participant "Entry (Envoy)\nvirtual IP of flight-ops" as EFO
box "flight-ops-n (the replica that answers)" #F7F7F7
participant "FlightUtilizationController" as FlightUtilizationController
participant "GenerateFlightUtilizationReportUseCase" as GenerateFlightUtilizationReportUseCase
database "own database" as DBFO
end box
collections "peer replicas\nflight-ops-m" as PFO
== GET /api/flights/reports/utilization ==
Actor -> EFO : GET /api/flights/reports/utilization\n(HTTPS, Authorization: Bearer JWT)
EFO -> FlightUtilizationController : to a ready replica\n(another one if it fails)
FlightUtilizationController -> GenerateFlightUtilizationReportUseCase : execute(...)
GenerateFlightUtilizationReportUseCase -> DBFO : own flights
GenerateFlightUtilizationReportUseCase -> PFO : GET /internal/replicas/flights\n(every peer in parallel)
PFO --> GenerateFlightUtilizationReportUseCase : their flights
GenerateFlightUtilizationReportUseCase -> GenerateFlightUtilizationReportUseCase : keep the latest change of each record,\nleave out deleted ones; filter, compute, sort, page
GenerateFlightUtilizationReportUseCase --> FlightUtilizationController : result
FlightUtilizationController --> Actor : 200 OK (X-Node-Id; X-Partial-Result if both holders of a record were unreachable)
@enduml
